fff}</style></head><body><main class="wrap"><div class="card"><div class="eyebrow">Reddott Films · <?=h($topic)?></div><h1><?=h($title)?></h1><p class="muted">Published on <?=h(substr($published,0,10))?> · This page is an editorial companion to the official Reddott Films video.</p></div><article class="card article"><?php if($thumb!==''):?><img src="<?=h($thumb)?>" alt="<?=h($title)?>" style="width:100%;border-radius:14px;display:block;margin-bottom:20px"><?php endif;?><div class="video"><iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/<?=h($id)?>" title="<?=h($title)?>" loading="lazy" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" allowfullscreen></iframe></div><h2>What this Reddott Films video is about</h2><p>This article accompanies <strong><?=h($title)?></strong> and is designed to give readers useful context before or after watching. The video remains the primary source for the visual and audio experience, while this page organizes the available information into an easier-to-read reference.</p><?php if($description!==''):?><h2>Creator-published description</h2><p><?=nl2br(h($description))?></p><?php endif;?><h2>What to look for while watching</h2><p>Because this is a <?=h($topic)?> piece, viewers can pay attention to how the title and published description connect with what is actually presented in the video. The most useful approach is to watch the full piece and compare the visual or narrative details with the creator's stated focus rather than relying on the title alone.</p><?php if($points):?><h2>Key points from the published information</h2><ul><?php foreach($points as $p):?><li><?=h($p)?></li><?php endforeach;?></ul><?php endif;?><h2>Why this companion page exists</h2><p>Reddott Films uses this space to add readable context around its video library instead of treating an embedded player as the entire article. If you are discovering the video from search, you can read the context here and then continue to the original YouTube video.</p><p><a class="btn" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=<?=rawurlencode($id)?>" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Watch on YouTube</a></p></article><div class="card source"><strong>Editorial note:</strong> This article uses the video's own published metadata and clearly separates that source information from the site's added context. Content with insufficient source material is intentionally kept out of search indexing until it receives additional editorial review.<br><br><a href="/Reddott-films/blogs/">← Back to Reddott Films Blog</a></div></main></body></html>
